{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Go standard library and existing Hyperledger Fabric protobuf definitions for underlying configuration structure management.",
    "Implement fluent API sub-types (e.g., Application, Channel, Orderer, Org) as light wrappers over underlying protobuf config groups to support method chaining.",
    "Extract Orderer configuration types into a dedicated `pkg/configtx/orderer` subpackage and MSP configuration types into `pkg/configtx/membership` subpackage.",
    "Refactor `SetXXX` behavior to perform upsert operations (overwrite existing map/slice entries without throwing errors when items exist).",
    "Refactor `RemoveXXX` methods to be idempotent, returning no errors when attempting to delete non-existent values.",
    "Build the CLI tool using a standard Go CLI framework (such as Cobra or standard `flag`/`os.Args`) under `cmd/configtx` to support genesis block, channel tx generation, and subcommands for config updates."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is familiar with Go, Protobuf, Hyperledger Fabric internals, and godoc formatting rules.",
    "Existing unit tests exist in `pkg/configtx` and will need refactoring to reflect the updated function signatures and behavior.",
    "No breaking protocol-level protobuf change is required; changes are confined to the high-level Go SDK/API surface in `pkg/configtx`."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "Refactor Set and Remove Semantics (U1 & U6)",
      "activity_description": "Convert all `AddXXX` and `UpdateXXX` functions to `SetXXX` with upsert/overwrite behavior (handling slices like `SetAnchorPeer` to prevent duplicates). Update `RemoveXXX` functions to be idempotent and return no error when non-existent items are removed. Update unit tests for these mutators.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "Package Namespacing Refactoring (U4 & U5)",
      "activity_description": "Create `orderer` and `membership` subpackages within `configtx`. Move Orderer types (Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState) and MSP types (SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs) into their respective packages. Update internal references and GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "API Renaming and Method Chaining Implementation (U2 & U3)",
      "activity_description": "Rename `Base()` to `BaseConfig()` and `Updated()` to `UpdatedConfig()`. Design and implement sub-type wrapper structs (e.g., Application, Orderer, Org) to enable chained calls like `c.Application().Org(orgName).SetAnchorPeer(...)`. Update tests for API chaining.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "GoDoc Polish and Examples Overhaul (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Enhance documentation for `New()`. Remove unnecessary capability/MSP examples and output validation comments. Rename and split example functions into focused examples (e.g., `Example_textExample`, `Example_policyRetrieval`, `Example_ordererUpdate`). Fix linebreaks to prevent horizontal scrolling in godoc output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "CLI Tool Development (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Create the `configtx` CLI application capable of generating system channel genesis blocks, application channel creation transactions, and config update transactions via subcommands and flags (e.g., `configtx update addAnchorPeer`). Include CLI documentation and help command support.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "End-to-End Testing & Verification",
      "activity_description": "Execute full package test suite, verify CLI binary execution against sample configurations, and inspect locally generated godoc web pages (`godoc -http=:2020`) for proper rendering and formatting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 14.5
  }
}
```

